**Given:**

Filling pipe = 12 hours

Emptying pipe = 21 hours

Tank should be half filled

**Formula used:**

Net work rate = (1/fill time) - (1/empty time)

Time = Work ÷ Rate

**Calculation:**

Filling rate = dfrac{1}{12}

Emptying rate = dfrac{1}{21}

Net rate = dfrac{1}{12} - dfrac{1}{21}

⇒ Net rate = dfrac{7 - 4}{84} = dfrac{3}{84} = dfrac{1}{28}

Work needed = half tank = dfrac{1}{2}

Time = dfrac{1/2}{1/28}

⇒ Time = 14 hours

**∴ The tank will be half filled in 14 hours.**

**Given:**

Speed of boat in the direction of stream = 47 km/hr

Speed of boat against the direction of stream = 19 km/hr

**Formula used:**

Speed of current = dfrac{{Speed downstream} - {Speed upstream}}{2}

**Calculation:**

{Speed of current} = dfrac{47 - 19}{2}

⇒ {Speed of current} = dfrac{28}{2}

⇒ Speed of current = 14 km/hr

**∴ The correct answer is option (2).**

